  "notes": "Arista 7280R data sheet, 'Arista 7280SR2K-48C6' bullet: \"7280SR2K-48C6: 24 port SFP+, 24 port 25GbE SFP and 6 ports 100GbE\" / \"Offers 48 wire speed SFP ports with 24 1/10G and 24 1/10/25G with FC and RS FEC\" / \"25G SFP ports offer 25G or 10G/1G speeds configurable in groups of 4\" / \"Six 100G QSFP ports allow choice of 6 x 100GbE, 24x 25GbE, 6x 40GbE, or 24x 10GbE\" / \"2.88Tbps of wire speed performance with 4GB of buffer\". The Model Comparison cell in the same sheet prints the two SFP groups in one order, \"24 x SFP25, 24 x SFP+\". ASSUMPTION, stated so it can be corrected: neither table prints front-panel numbering, so Ethernet1-24 is modelled as the 25G (SFP28) group and Ethernet25-48 as the SFP+ group, following the vendor's own Ports-cell order. If a unit numbers them the other way round, the two groups swap and nothing else about the box changes. The comparison table flags this SKU End of Sale (E)."
